# vectorlib: shapes drawn smooth onto pixels. Paths of lines, curves and arcs (and SVG's path
# data), moved, turned and scaled by a matrix; filled by either rule, or outlined with joins,
# caps and dashes; with a color, a gradient or an image; kept within a box or another shape. It
# draws onto pixels the program gives it, 0xAARRGGBB, and touches nothing else.
#
#   phi build vectorlib.phi --library      # vectorlib.philib, which a program includes with `use vectorlib;`
#
# README.md says which names are its API.

use vectorlib.geometry;
use vectorlib.path;
use vectorlib.paint;
use vectorlib.canvas;

phi.VectorLib:Library
{
	const int VERSION: 1;

	# Call this once, before anything else in the library. There's nothing to set up yet, but a
	# program that calls it keeps working when there is.
	[Start]
	[end]
}
